# Normalise line endings so a checkout is byte-identical on every platform.
* text=auto eol=lf

# The miner descriptor is HASHED, not merely read.
#
# `registerMiner()` commits the SHA-256 of these exact bytes on-chain, and every
# Telegraph node recomputes that hash over the YAML it fetches from `base_url`.
# The two must agree or the miner fails verification while appearing perfectly
# healthy — it serves prices normally and nothing in its logs explains the
# rejection.
#
# This is not hypothetical. A Windows checkout with core.autocrlf=true rewrote
# this file's endings to CRLF, adding 161 bytes: `npm run yaml:hash` reported
# 67b5fab0… from the working copy while the Linux container served 8e485af6…
# from the repo bytes. Pinning the file to LF keeps working copy, repo, and
# deployed image in agreement, so the hash is the same wherever it is computed.
*.yaml text eol=lf
*.yml  text eol=lf

# Binary assets must never be line-ending converted.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.svg text eol=lf
